# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Copy to .env.local. Nothing here is required: with an empty file the app runs
#  on an embedded Postgres with mock providers, and the whole test suite passes.
#  Check what is actually configured at /preflight.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#  NSE Copilot uses SIX of the variables below and nothing else. The rest of this
#  file is the template's full catalogue, kept because it documents what each
#  unset value falls back to — but adding a second LLM provider, an embedding key
#  or a Tavily key is a spec violation here, not an upgrade (§4.1: one provider,
#  one database, one host).
#
#  The target .env.local, in full:
#
#      GEMINI_API_KEY=            # the one key; blank is supported (mock mode)
#      LLM_MODE=mock              # `live` once the key is filled in
#      LLM_PRIMARY=gemini-2.5-flash
#      LLM_FALLBACKS=             # EMPTY ON PURPOSE — see the note below
#      LLM_CACHE=on
#      ML_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:8000
#
#  LLM_FALLBACKS being present-and-empty is load-bearing. It is the one variable
#  in the codebase where blank differs from absent: absent keeps the template's
#  default chain, empty means NO fallbacks. Left to the ordinary `env()` helper an
#  empty value would restore a chain ending in Anthropic and Groq models whose
#  keys are deliberately unset, and every live turn would attempt two unreachable
#  providers before falling through to the mock. See fallbackModels() in
#  src/lib/llm/router.ts and the tests in tests/honesty.test.ts.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Database ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Leave unset for local work: the app runs PGlite (Postgres compiled to WASM,
# with pgvector) against ./.pglite and migrates itself on first connect.
# Set it to a Neon connection string for deployment — serverless needs a real
# database, and the embedded one is per-process.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:pass@ep-xxx.region.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require
# Where the embedded database keeps its files. `memory://` keeps it in RAM.
# PGLITE_DIR=.pglite

# ── Model providers ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# THIS BUILD USES GEMINI ONLY (§4.1). With no key, LLM_MODE falls back to `mock`
# and the whole app — including the test suite and the eval runner — still works.
# aistudio.google.com/apikey, free tier is enough.
# GEMINI_API_KEY=...
#
# Do not set these two. They are the template's other providers; this project is
# a single-provider build and tests/honesty.test.ts asserts the chain stays
# Gemini-only.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# GROQ_API_KEY=gsk_...

# ── Model routing ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# mock   — never calls a model; deterministic, offline, demo-safe
# cached — serves from the response cache, calls a model on a miss
# live   — calls a model (the default as soon as a key above is set)
# LLM_MODE=live
# The chain, tried in order. Model ids are never hard-coded in the source.
# LLM_PRIMARY=gemini-2.5-flash
# Set this to EMPTY (the bare name and an equals sign, no value) for Gemini-only.
# Commenting it out is NOT the same thing: absent restores the default chain.
# LLM_FALLBACKS=
# Response cache: `off` disables reads and writes. Keep it on to rehearse a demo.
# LLM_CACHE=on
# Per-session ceilings, so a tool loop cannot exhaust a free tier mid-demo. Sized for a
# whole conversation: a session is long-lived, and a ceiling sized for one turn makes every
# later turn fall back silently. agent.maxSteps in idea.config.ts bounds a single turn.
# LLM_MAX_CALLS_PER_SESSION=120
# LLM_MAX_TOOL_STEPS=60
# LLM_MAX_TOKENS_PER_SESSION=500000
# An OpenAI-compatible endpoint other than Groq (Together, Fireworks, OpenRouter…).
# GROQ_BASE_URL=https://api.groq.com/openai/v1

# ── Embeddings ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LEAVE ALL OF THESE UNSET (§4.1). Unset means deterministic local embeddings,
# and memory and retrieval work without a key.
# EMBED_PROVIDER=voyage
# VOYAGE_API_KEY=pa-...
# EMBED_PROVIDER=openai
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
# EMBED_MODEL=voyage-3-lite

# ── The ML service ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Where the FastAPI model service lives. Start it with `python ml/tasks.py serve`.
# Unreachable is a supported state: the signals, model card and evidence pages
# show an explicit error naming the missing service rather than inventing figures.
ML_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:8000
# How long to wait before calling the service down.
# ML_TIMEOUT_MS=5000
#
# Set on the SERVICE (not here) when deploying, or the browser blocks every call
# with nothing in the server logs to explain it. Defaults to localhost:3000.
# COPILOT_CORS_ORIGINS=https://your-app.vercel.app

# ── Tools ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LEAVE UNSET. `web_search` is deliberately absent from agent.enabledTools: with
# no key it returns results labelled MOCK, and a mock search result inside a
# financial answer is a risk with no upside.
# TAVILY_API_KEY=tvly-...

# ── Connectors (the partner-tool integration slot) ──────────────────────────
# Each is enabled only when its keys are present. Approvals fall back to the
# local outbox otherwise, so the demo works with none of these.
# GITHUB_TOKEN=ghp_...
# GITHUB_REPO=owner/name
# NOTION_TOKEN=secret_...
# NOTION_DATABASE_ID=...
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_...
# RESEND_FROM=you@yourdomain.com
# SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL=https://hooks.slack.com/services/...

# ── Auth (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The app works signed out; a demo should not open with a login wall. Set these
# only if the idea needs accounts. With a real DATABASE_URL sessions are stored
# in Postgres; on the embedded database they are JWTs.
# AUTH_SECRET=generate-with-openssl-rand-base64-32
# AUTH_GOOGLE_ID=...
# AUTH_GOOGLE_SECRET=...
# Deployed host only. Keep commented locally: an empty value counts as set and
# switches host trust off.
# AUTH_URL=https://your-app.vercel.app
# Only for `npm start` on localhost; Vercel provides it in production.
# AUTH_TRUST_HOST=true

# ── Scheduler ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Without this, /api/cron is unauthenticated. Fine locally; set it before deploying.
# CRON_SECRET=generate-with-openssl-rand-base64-32

# ── Hero 3D scene (optional) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The hero has a slot for a Spline scene and ships without one — the original's
# artwork belonged to another project. Unset, nothing is fetched and the hero
# uses its animated orb instead. To add one: export from Spline, drop the file in
# public/, and point this at it.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_HERO_SCENE_URL=/hero-scene.splinecode
# Only if you vendor the runtime's wasm modules rather than using Spline's CDN.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_HERO_SCENE_WASM_PATH=/spline

# ── Site ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Used for absolute URLs in metadata and the OG image.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://your-app.vercel.app
